# Kardinal Project Rules

## Deployment

- **GitHub Actions is already configured** (`.github/workflows/docker-build.yml`)
- When the user makes changes, remind them that they only need to:
  1. Commit and push to GitHub
  2. GitHub Actions will automatically build and push the Docker image
  3. The server's cron job will automatically pull and restart at the next scheduled run (02:00 daily by default)
- For a faster rollout, the user can SSH into the server and run `/srv/kardinal/update-kardinal.sh` manually
- No manual Docker build/push steps are needed unless testing locally
- The workflow uses GitHub Actions cache and handles both pushes and PRs

## Health Endpoint

- A `/health` endpoint exists at `https://kardinal.nvdh.dev/health`
- Through the proxy it returns only `{"status": "ok"}`
- From inside the container (the Docker healthcheck, `docker exec kardinal python -c ...` against `http://127.0.0.1:5000/health`) it also returns:
  - `deployed_at`: timestamp when the container was deployed (useful for verifying updates)
  - `markdown_accessible`: whether the markdown file can be read (not just that it exists)

## Performance

- Wikilink lookups and page renders are cached and bounded:
  - Rendered board cached per worker for 60 s, served stale while one background thread refreshes (`KARDINAL_PAGE_CACHE_TTL`)
  - In-memory caching of definitive lookup results (1000 entries, 1 hour); failed lookups are cached for 60 s
  - Parallel lookups through a pool of 8, with a 4 s total budget per render
- A page view costs at most one lookup per unique wikilink per minute, instead of 25-40 on every request
